{
  // ==========================================================================
  // AGM PROPOSAL — PLAZA 600  ·  Cloudflare Worker with static assets
  // --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // The static proposal lives in ./public and is served through the Worker in
  // ./src/index.js, which enforces the password gate.
  //
  // "run_worker_first": true is LOAD-BEARING. Without it Cloudflare's asset
  // server answers requests for ./public files directly and the Worker never
  // runs — which would publish the proposal with no password screen at all.
  // Do not remove it.
  // ==========================================================================
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "600-building-proposal",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-02",

  "assets": {
    "directory": "./public",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "run_worker_first": true
  },

  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },

  // The *.workers.dev URL, deliberately ON.
  //
  // The proposal is reached through a branded Wix link
  // (www.agmrealestategroup.com/plaza600proposal) that REDIRECTS here. It must
  // not be reached through a Wix iframe or a masked/cloaked redirect: this
  // Worker answers on workers.dev, workers.dev is on the Public Suffix List, so
  // every *.workers.dev subdomain is its own registrable site. Framed on
  // agmrealestategroup.com that is cross-site, the session cookie becomes a
  // third-party cookie, and browsers drop it — the password is accepted and the
  // visitor lands back on the cover page with no error. See "Embedding" in
  // README.md.
  //
  // A plain redirect avoids all of that: the visitor arrives top-level, so the
  // cookie is first-party. Turning this off would break that link. Only set it
  // false after a real custom domain is attached and serving, which requires
  // the zone to be on Cloudflare.
  "workers_dev": true,

  // Per-version Preview URLs are ON. This is the Workers equivalent of a Pages
  // branch preview: `wrangler versions upload` creates a version that is NOT
  // serving production traffic and gives it its own URL to review.
  // The gate applies to preview URLs exactly as it does to production, because
  // run_worker_first makes the Worker handle every request on every hostname.
  // Set false to stop issuing them.
  "preview_urls": true

  // Secrets are NOT set here — they are encrypted Cloudflare secrets.
  //   npx wrangler secret put SITE_PASSWORD
  //   npx wrangler secret put GATE_SECRET
  // Optional analytics (plain vars are fine):
  //   POSTHOG_KEY, POSTHOG_HOST
  // For local development put all of them in .dev.vars (git-ignored).
}
